issue.description:
Reposition the existing Delete theme action so it no longer sits beside the theme selector/name on the left side of the header.

## Goal

Make the header hierarchy clearer by grouping Delete with the other theme-level utility actions while keeping destructive behavior visually separated from constructive actions such as Export and Save.

## Change

Move the existing Delete theme control into the right-side header utility cluster.

Preferred order:

* Delete theme
* vertical divider
* dark mode toggle
* undo
* redo
* reset
* export
* save

Delete should sit immediately to the left of the dark mode toggle, with a vertical divider separating it from the rest of the utility controls.

## Delete control

Keep Delete as an icon-only action if that matches the existing header control language.

Requirements:

* use the existing delete/trash icon;
* accessible name: **Delete theme**;
* tooltip: **Delete theme**;
* retain existing delete behavior and confirmation flow;
* use the existing destructive hover/focus treatment if available;
* do not make the action visually dominant in its resting state.

## Divider

Add a subtle vertical divider between Delete and the dark mode toggle.

Requirements:

* use an existing semantic border/divider token;
* keep the divider visually restrained;
* align it with the current header height and spacing rhythm;
* do not introduce a new custom color or spacing token.

## Remove old placement

Remove the Delete control from its current position beside the theme selector/name.

Preserve:

* theme selector/name behavior;
* dropdown behavior;
* built-in/custom theme semantics;
* current header height;
* dark mode toggle behavior;
* undo/redo/reset/export/save behavior.

## Safety / interaction

Do not:

* change delete semantics;
* remove confirmation;
* allow built-in themes to become deletable if they are not currently deletable;
* change Save/Export placement;
* place Delete next to Save or Export;
* change persistence/history behavior;
* add dependencies or network behavior.

## Accessibility

Verify:

* icon-only Delete has an accessible name;
* tooltip is available;
* keyboard focus order follows visual order;
* destructive focus/hover remains perceivable;
* confirmation remains keyboard accessible;
* divider is decorative/non-interactive.

## Acceptance

* Delete theme is removed from the left-side theme selector area.
* Delete theme appears immediately left of the dark mode toggle in the right-side utility cluster.
* A subtle vertical divider separates Delete from the dark mode toggle.
* Delete remains icon-only, accessible, and confirmed before execution.
* Existing theme selector, dark mode, undo/redo/reset, Export, Save, persistence, and theme semantics remain unchanged.
* No dependency, network, schema, or public API changes are introduced.
